    "description": "Use money-time points when partners enter or leave a business at different times.",
    "teachingApproach": "Give every rupee a clock: one rupee invested for one month earns one money-month point. Start with equal capital for unequal times, then late joins, early exits and three-person timelines. Make 'joined after x months' translate immediately into 'worked for total months minus x'. Close with equal-profit and share-difference questions that show why capital alone is no longer enough.",
